<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barbara Allen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century or earlier; first mentioned 2 January <a href="/years/1666">1666</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Barbara Allen&quot; (Child 84, Roud 54) is a traditional ballad that began in the 17th century or earlier. The earliest surviving mention is in the diary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-pepys">Samuel Pepys</a> for 2 January 1666, who at a New Year's party delighted in hearing the actress and singer Elizabeth Knepp sing &quot;her little Scotch song of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> Allen&quot;.</p></div>
